## Tell us about a problem

If something in {{ project_name }} is hard or impossible for you to use, email
[{{ author_email }}](mailto:{{ author_email }}).
{%- if public %} You can also
[open an issue on GitHub](https://github.com/{{ github_user }}/{{ slug }}/issues/new), but you do not
need a GitHub account to report a problem.
{%- endif %}

Say what you were trying to do, what happened, and which browser and assistive technology you use,
if any. You will get a reply within 10 working days. If you need content from {{ project_name }} in
another format, ask, and we will send it.

## How we check

- **Automated scan.** The end-to-end tests run [axe-core](https://github.com/dequelabs/axe-core)
  with the WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2 level A and AA rules and axe's best practices, on every page,
  in the light and the dark theme. See
  {{ file('tests/e2e/a11y.spec.ts') }}.
- **Reflow.** Every page is loaded 320 px wide and fails if it scrolls sideways. See
  {{ file('tests/e2e/reflow.spec.ts') }}.
- **Lint.** [Biome's accessibility rules](https://biomejs.dev/linter/javascript/rules/#a11y) check
  every change for things like missing alt text, invalid ARIA and click handlers without a keyboard
  equivalent.
- **This statement.**
  {{ file('tests/e2e/accessibility-statement.spec.ts') }}
  fails when this page loses a section, claims a status it has not earned, loses its email contact,
  or goes more than 400 days without a review.

All of this runs on every pull request. Automated tools find only part of the problems a person
can run into, so a passing run does not mean there are none.

Not checked yet: nobody has used {{ project_name }} with the keyboard alone or with a screen reader
to check it by hand.

